From 7e47f25508d581424b2d2bb225d3f1ed6f9ec695 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:24:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FEX: draw probe with D2R-sized draws, keeps its device

fex26's 8-pixel triangles finish so fast that what changes between draws
shows less than in the game (0.4-1.6 us a draw against 2-6 us in D2R's
passes). Every test now draws 1000 meshes of 220 triangles (440 vertices,
660 indices), one per cell of a 40 x 25 grid so they cover the target
once: into 1280x720 R11G11B10F + RGBA8 + D24S8 with a lit pixel shader
(2 texture reads from an array of 8, 8 lights; like D2R's main pass,
~920 pixels a draw), and into a 2048x2048 D16 map with an alpha-test
pixel shader (like its shadow passes, ~4,200 pixels a draw). Per kind:
no changes, like D2R (new push constants and 2 new root constant buffers
every draw), first instance and one multi-draw call (each draw finds its
block in a buffer, material, lights and texture index read per pixel).

With fex24 and fex26 the game died right after the last test, when the
probe tore its device down. The probe now never destroys or frees
anything it made; its objects (~35 MB of GPU memory) stay until the game
ends.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WZVGoVEaHJ78mpf2D3MiER
